Package: librnnoise-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: recurrent neural network for audio noise suppression (Telegram fork)
 RNNoise suppresses background noise in voice calls. This is the desktop-app
 fork used by Telegram Desktop, which prefixes the library's internal symbols
 so it can be linked alongside the copy embedded in tg_owt without colliding.
 .
 Telegram Desktop requires this via pkg-config and links it unconditionally
 through tgcalls. Ubuntu ships no rnnoise of its own.
 .
 This package provides a static library, its header and a pkg-config file.
 Upstream installs only a CMake package configuration, so the pkg-config file
 is generated during packaging.
